s", "Conversation data kept to what safety review needs, with access limited and logged"], "tags": ["ai", "governance", "llm"], "keywords": ["AI chatbot online safety Canada", "Bill C-34 Safe Social Media Act", "Digital Safety Commission of Canada", "AI chatbot crisis escalation", "manipulative engagement AI companion", "youth AI chatbot safety", "edtech AI study companion", "LLM safety evaluation", "Digital Safety Plan", "fractional CTO Canada"], "faq": [["What would Canada's proposed law require from AI chatbot services?", "Bill C-34, introduced in June 2026 and not yet law, proposes a duty for AI chatbot services to mitigate the risk of harmful content, put emergency measures in place for crisis situations and mitigate harmful chatbot behaviour, with a Digital Safety Commission to oversee compliance."], ["How should an AI chatbot handle a user in crisis?", "Detect crisis signals on every message, switch to a fixed, tested response that gives crisis resources such as Canada's 9-8-8 line, route the case to trained people where the service offers that, and never let the model improvise in those moments."], ["What counts as manipulative engagement in a chatbot?", "Design that encourages emotional dependence or keeps people engaged against their interests, such as a companion persona that guilts users for leaving. The safest approach is to review every engagement feature against the user's interests, not only retention."]], "related": ["/ai-architect/", "/fractional-cto/", "/regions/"], "citations": [{"title": "Bill C-34, the Safe Social Media Act", "url": "https://www.canada.ca/en/canadian-heritage/services/safe-social-media-act.html", "publisher": "Government of Canada", "date": "2026"}, {"title": "Bill C-34: Canada proposes legislation to regulate social media, AI chatbot, and online services", "url": "https://www.torys.com/our-latest-thinking/publications/2026/06/bill-c-34", "publisher": "Torys", "date": "Jun 2026"}, {"title": "Bill C-34 at a glance: Canada's new 